          "quote": "NbMoZrTiV LRHEA specimens were prepared by vacuum arc melting. The purity of the Nb, Mo, Zr, Ti and V metal particles was 99.9%. To protect the metal material from oxidation during the melting process, the chamber must first be vacuumed to a vacuum level of 1 × 10 4 Pa. High purity Ar gas is passed through, and the Ti alloy is melted by the induced arc to further remove the oxygen in the chamber. Due to the presence of refractory metal elements, the alloy ingots are repeatedly melted at least eight times to ensure a homogeneous composition.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
